  </Metadata>
  <Document>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="Normal" BlockID="73025342-15c0-41f1-bcd5-33029cbd7675">
      <Normal>
        <Normal>
          <Normal>The fallen Egyptian laborer, Shoukry Waheed, forced to work for the british army in the levant region. He was there because the british needed men for heavy railway construction. </Normal>
        </Normal>
      </Normal>
    </ParagraphLine>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="Normal" BlockID="48dd6062-8098-4f91-b5e1-e0c81d268d86">
      <Normal>
        <Normal>
          <Normal>It's not surprising for an Egyptian to be there as Egypt was under the british occupation and the Egyptians were the best and had high tolerance for the inhumane construction work.</Normal>
        </Normal>
      </Normal>
    </ParagraphLine>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="List">
      <List>
        <ListItem BlockID="7bc80fa4-fddd-4810-b162-93b6c7d4807b">
          <Normal>
            <Normal>
              <Normal>Talk about that Shoukry ended up here because he needed money for his family as the conditions don't look great there.</Normal>
            </Normal>
          </Normal>
        </ListItem>
        <ListItem BlockID="8b863e9c-206d-406e-8428-8a9cffde5ae5">
          <Normal>
            <Normal>
              <Normal>Talk about that a newcomer Ali came and he told him during work that the condition is worsening in Egypt and a new drug is taking the country by storm.</Normal>
            </Normal>
          </Normal>
        </ListItem>
        <ListItem BlockID="9d68d4fe-3580-44dd-8196-f269c164ae8a">
          <Normal>
            <Normal>
              <Normal>One day Shoukry unfortunately died because of exhaustion, and Ali, our playable character, discover the letter that Shoukry wrote for his wife.</Normal>
            </Normal>
          </Normal>
        </ListItem>
        <ListItem BlockID="f504af49-2146-4741-a6af-8940f0823053">
          <Normal>
            <Normal>
              <Normal>Shoukry with two young men Ali, Khaled, and they reminded him of his sons.</Normal>
            </Normal>
          </Normal>
        </ListItem>
      </List>
    </ParagraphLine>
  </Document>
  <Localization />
</File>